class Solution {
public:
    ListNode* mergeTwoLists(ListNode* l1, ListNode* l2) {
        ListNode dummy;
        ListNode* tail = &dummy;

        while(l1 && l2){
            if(l1->val < l2->val){
                tail->next = l1;
                l1 = l1->next;
            }
            else{
                tail->next = l2;
                l2 = l2->next;
            }
            tail = tail->next;
        }

        tail->next = l1 ? l1 : l2;
        return dummy.next;
    }
};
**Intuition:**  
Both linked lists are already sorted.  
Compare their current nodes and always choose the smaller one.

**Algorithm:**  
Use a dummy node and move through both lists.  
Attach the smaller node to the result until one list is empty.  
Attach the remaining nodes at the end.

**Complexity:**  
Time: **O(n + m)**  
Space: **O(1)**
